X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2476138-moses-man-finding-home"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:Moses Man: Finding Home
DTSTART:20261115T000000Z
DTEND:20261115T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261112T133008Z
UID:20261115T000000Z-2482450@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261115T000000Z
CATEGORIES:Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Written by Deborah Haber\, directed by Joe Calarco\, with musi
 cal direction by Casey Filiaci\, "Moses Man: Finding Home" presents the tr
 ue story of Haber's parents who fled their home in Vienna\, spending years
  as refugees in Cyprus\, Palestine\, Nyasaland\, and South Africa\, before
  finally finding a new home in the United States.&#160\; The play explores
  the themes of forced displacement and migration by connecting Haber's par
 ents' story to recent refugee stories.&#160\; Still in development\, the e
 vening will feature a dramatic reading of the musical.&#160\; Cosponsored 
 by the Center for the Study of the Middle East and the Center for Caribbea
 n and Latin American Studies\, with additional support from the IU Institu
 te for Advanced Study and the College Arts &amp\; Humanities Institute\, t
 he African Studies Program\, the Borns Jewish Studies Program\, and the In
 stitute for European Studies.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112T183008Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2476138-moses-man-finding-home
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Written by Deborah Haber\, directed by J
 oe Calarco\, with musical direction by Casey Filiaci\, "Moses Man: Finding
  Home" presents the true story of Haber's parents who fled their home in V
 ienna\, spending years as refugees in Cyprus\, Palestine\, Nyasaland\, and
  South Africa\, before finally finding a new home in the United States.&#1
 60\; The play explores the themes of forced displacement and migration by 
 connecting Haber's parents' story to recent refugee stories.&#160\; Still 
 in development\, the evening will feature a dramatic reading of the musica
 l.&#160\; Cosponsored by the Center for the Study of the Middle East and t
 he Center for Caribbean and Latin American Studies\, with additional suppo
 rt from the IU Institute for Advanced Study and the College Arts &amp\; Hu
 manities Institute\, the African Studies Program\, the Borns Jewish Studie
 s Program\, and the Institute for European Studies.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>pearsonc@iu.edu</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2482450
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>Moses Man: Finding Home tells the true stories of f
 orcibly displaced people: from the Holocaust\, from civil war\, from viole
 nce.&#160\; This presentation of Deborah Haber's musical\, a show that exa
 mines the universality of displacement and the fragility of belonging by w
 eaving the true story of the Haber family fleeing Vienna during WWII with 
 the story of present-day Syrian and African refugees.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
END:VEVENT
