 , where he studies with Anne Epperson. He earned a bachelor's degree in p
 iano performance from Kookmin University in Seoul\, South Korea\, graduat
 ing with top honors in performance. He subsequently completed the Artist 
 Diploma program in Collaborative Piano at the Korea National University o
 f Arts. In 2022 and 2023\, Song was selected to participate in the collab
 orative piano program at the Music Academy of the West in Santa Barbara\,
  California\, where he received full scholarship. Prior to his studies in
  the United States\, he was active as a professional collaborative pianis
 t in South Korea\, performing with distinguished musicians including viol
 inist Sung-Ju Lee\, violinist Ju-Young Baek\, violinist Jehye Lee\, violi
 st Richard Yongjae O'Neill\, and violinist Dayoon You\, among others. Thr
