  account for a growing share of documented murder victims and examine how 
 the geography of recorded violence has shifted. I then assess two policies
 : Pará's land registration mandate\, which was followed by fewer recorded
  threats and conflicts\, and Brazil's priority municipality program\, whic
 h substantially reduced deforestation. The evidence for the program's soci
 al benefits is less certain because estimates of violence depend on which 
 municipalities are used for comparison. Together\, the studies show why ev
 aluating environmental policy requires careful attention to both the limit
 s of violence records and the reasons places were selected for interventio
