DESCRIPTION:12-1 p.m. Lunch\, Martin Commons\, second floor1–2 p.m. Arti
 st talk\, Learn more about Susan's artistic journey\, creative philosophy
 \, and evolving practice\, followed by an open Q+A session\, Martin Common
 s\, second floor2–4 p.m. Enjoy hands-on artist programming and a rare lo
 ok at selected objects from the museum's collections.  Susan Charlesworth 
 is an award-winning basket weaver who first began weaving in 2005\, when s
 he entered her baskets into the Choctaw Nation Annual Labor Day Festival a
 nd Art Show. Susan has continued to receive awards at multiple Native art 
 markets\, including the Eiteljorg Indian Market &amp\; Festival. Susan is 
 a retired CNA and social service consultant with a master's degree in soci
 al work and an avid volunteer with the Alzheimer's Association. She now se
 rves as an Alzheimer's Association Community Educator in Indianapolis.All 
 of these activities are free and open to the public. This program is co-or
 ganized by the IU First Nations Educational and Cultural Center and the Es
 kenazi Museum of Art\, with support from the Eiteljorg Museum of American 
 Indians and Western Art.
