ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1066,1067/28852_xxdevelopment_events_hopefamily_04262022_
 212_o3.rev.1761853853.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Health and wellness
DESCRIPTION:Parents' Night In offers a unique opportunity to enjoy the mus
 eum with separate but parallel programming for kids and adults that suppor
 ts connection\, creativity\, and relaxation.K-12 Children's Program: Guide
 d gallery exploration\, hands-on art activity in the art studio + snack.Ad
 ult Program: Choose your own adventure! Wander the galleries with a self-g
 uided activity for connection or join the guided tour. Enjoy art-making in
  the 2nd floor atrium and a sweet treat and tea.Know Before You Go: Read a
 bout where to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guideli
 nes.When You Arrive:If you parked in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services 
 can validate your parking voucher for a 40% discount.  Head upstairs to th
 e 2nd Floor and into the Simpson Center for Education to start.  When in t
 he galleries\, do not touch the artwork. Be mindful to keep body parts and
  anything you're carrying at least 18" away from the art.  Photography is 
 welcome! Just no flash or selfie sticks.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021T195209Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2457788-parents-evening-in-at-the-es
 kenazi-museum-of-art
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Parents' Night In</em> offers a unique
  opportunity to enjoy the museum with separate but parallel programming fo
 r kids and adults that supports connection\, creativity\, and relaxation.<
 /p><p><strong>K-12 Children's Program:</strong> Guided gallery exploration
 \, hands-on art activity in the art studio + snack.</p><p><strong>Adult Pr
 ogram:</strong> Choose your own adventure! Wander the galleries with a sel
 f-guided activity for connection or join the guided tour. Enjoy art-making
  in the 2nd floor atrium and a sweet treat and tea.</p><p><strong>Know Bef
 ore You Go:</strong> Read about <a class="external" href="https://artmuseu
 m.indiana.edu/visit/your-visit.html"><span data-contrast="none">where to f
 ind us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines</span></a><
 span data-contrast="auto">.</span></p><p><strong>When You Arrive:</strong>
 </p><ul><li>If you parked in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services can vali
 date your parking voucher for a 40% discount.  </li><li>Head upstairs to t
 he 2nd Floor and into the Simpson Center for Education to start.  </li><li
 >When in the galleries\, do not touch the artwork. Be mindful to keep body
  parts and anything you're carrying at least 18" away from the art.  </li>
 <li>Photography is welcome! Just no flash or selfie sticks.  </li></ul>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Emily Zarse<br />\n  Public Experiences Ma
 nager<br />\n  eczarse@iu.edu\n</p>
