BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visit Bloomington": "https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/treasures-of-the-silk-road/59604/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:Treasures of the Silk Road
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261130T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261130T180000
UID:5a91f125fab3b3da7a9188aad4d58aac@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The McCalla Center\, in collaboration with musician and schola
 r Shahyar Daneshgar\, celebrates the opening of its new exhibition Treasur
 es of the Silk Road on Friday\, September 25th\, 4:00 pm-6:00 pm EDT.\nThe
  exhibit features over 70 musical instruments from the Pastel-Daneshgar mu
 sical instrument collection\, with a focus on strings\, flutes\, and percu
 ssion from across Asia\, the Middle East\, and North Africa. Crafted from 
 wood\, snakeskin\, horsehair\, lambskin\, camel bone\, and other unique ma
 terials\, these instruments provide a compelling history of cultural and a
 rtistic exchanges that have led to the myriad musical sounds and styles th
 at permeate the world today. The opening event will feature remarks from t
 he collection owner\, Shahyar Daneshgar\, and will feature musical clips p
 rovided by the Lotus World Music & Arts Festival.\nShahyar Daneshgar is a 
 lifelong musician\, scholar\, and cultural ambassador whose passion for tr
 aditional music has shaped more than three decades of collecting\, teachin
 g\, and performing. Born into a large musical family\, he studied at the T
 ehran Conservatory of Music before pursuing academic work in Germany and l
 ater at Indiana University\, where he earned his Ph.D. in Central Eurasian
  Studies in 1995. He taught at Indiana University until his retirement in 
 2024. He is founder and director of the Bloomington Silk Road Ensemble.\nT
 he exhibition is free and runs from September 25\, 2026\, to September 202
 7.\nThe mission of the McCalla Center is to provide accessible exhibition 
 and educational experiences\, creating opportunities for students\, facult
 y\, and the community to engage with collections\, IU-generated creative a
 ctivity\, and community projects in meaningful and innovative ways.
GEO:39.1709246;-86.527549
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th Street\, Bloomington
 \, IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/treasures-of-the-silk-road/5960
 4/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 237": "https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2392370-rainbow-connection"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_237
SUMMARY:Rainbow Connection
DTSTART:20261130T163000Z
DTEND:20261130T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260824T133911Z
UID:20261116T163000Z-2392370@events.iu.edu__20261130
CATEGORIES:Health and wellness
DESCRIPTION:Rainbow Connection offers a free\, confidential space for anyo
 ne under the LGBTQ+ umbrella to find community\, explore topics related to
  their identities\, learn about mental health topics\, or just have a week
 ly reset. This is a drop-in support group that does not require students t
 o sign up to participate.9/28 – "who I am" person drawing/talk about val
 ues and identity  10/5 – fall break intentions list/talk about self-care
  and goals  10/12 – mandalas/talk about mindfulness  10/19 - decorate a 
 "worth jar"/talk about gratitude and self-worth  10/26 – Winter Boos/ ta
 lk about self-care  11/2 – expressive art/talk about emotion regulation 
  11/9 – decorate tote bags  11/6 - stress balls/talk about stress manage
 ment  11/23 (Thanksgiving break) not meeting  11/30 – sensory jars/talk 
 about stress management and mindfulness  12/7 – coping toolboxAll Indian
 a University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultural\, and h
 istorical observances welcome all members of the Indiana University commun
 ity.
GEO:39.168722;-86.525274
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T141826Z
LOCATION:LGBTQ+ CULTURE CENTER
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lgbtq/event/2392370-rainbow-connection
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-teams="true">Rainbow Connection
  offers a free\, confidential space for anyone under the LGBTQ+ umbrella t
 o find community\, explore topics related to their identities\, learn abou
 t mental health topics\, or just have a weekly reset. This is a drop-in su
 pport group that does not require students to sign up to participate.</spa
 n></p><p class="x_MsoNormal"><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">9/28
  – "who I am" person drawing/talk about values and identity</span></p><p
  class="x_MsoNormal">  10/5 – fall break intentions list/talk about self
 -care and goals</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  10/12 – mandalas/talk about 
 mindfulness</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  10/19 - decorate a "worth jar"/tal
 k about gratitude and self-worth</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  10/26 – Win
 ter Boos/ talk about self-care</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  11/2 – expres
 sive art/talk about emotion regulation</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  11/9 
 – decorate tote bags</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  11/6 - stress balls/tal
 k about stress management</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  11/23 (Thanksgiving 
 break) not meeting</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  11/30 – sensory jars/talk
  about stress management and mindfulness</p><p class="x_MsoNormal">  12/7 
 – coping toolbox</p><p><span data-teams="true"><strong>All Indiana Unive
 rsity events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultural\, and historic
 al observances welcome all members of the Indiana University community.</s
 trong></span></p>
