 /src_region/0,0,768,768/33032_2-thumbnail-WEB.rev.1791831052.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Today's 60-minute Virtual Information Session will offer guida
 nce on crafting your application and an opportunity to interact with and p
 ose questions to Miller Program Director Daniel Martinez.  The J. Irwin Mi
 ller Master of Architecture program is a three-year in-residence program\,
  with a two-year advanced placement track possible for students who hold a
  B.Arch from a NAAB-accredited institution or regional equivalent. With ou
 r twin studios approach\, students take visual art course alongside archit
 ectural studios to develop their style of architectural design. The three-
 year program welcome applicants from a variety of educational and career b
 ackgrounds.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261012T185308Z
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2447912-miller-architecture-progr
 am-virtual-info-session-cra
