SUMMARY:Wellness Walk
DTSTART:20261203T223000Z
DTEND:20261203T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261012T114635Z
UID:20261203T223000Z-2447850@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261203T223000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,640,427/26885_xxbuilding_architectural_bradfeinknopf_0117
 2020_5_o4.rev.1750861000.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Functions, festivals, and celebratio
 ns
DESCRIPTION:This guided wellness walk explores 3 to 4 galleries. We offer 
 a series of prompts and activities centered around using the museum for we
 llness: finding comfort\, noticing by slowing down\, encouraging flexibili
 ty and curiosity\, and reflection. Participants can spend time independent
 ly with artworks\, with optional opportunities to share reflections and in
 sights along the way. No art experience required\, just a willingness to p
 ause\, notice\, and explore.About Your Guide  Leanne Anirudhan (she/her) i
 s a third year undergraduate student majoring in Social Work with a minor 
 in Counseling. Her passion for art and music was fostered by a high school
  ceramics teacher who regularly brought students to the Eskenazi Museum of
  Art. Outside of touring\, she loves hiking with her dog\, and playing gui
 tar. &#160\;Know Before You GoWalk-ins are welcome if there's space. To re
 serve a space\, RSVP below.Plan to arrive at least 5 minutes beforehand to
  check in and get ready.A small handbag may be carried at your side. Large
 r bags and backpacks must be stored before touring. Free lockers are avail
 able.Where to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guideli
 nesWhen You ArriveCheck in with Guest Services staff on the first floor.Ph
 otography is welcome\, without flash or selfie stick.Please do not touch a
 rtwork.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261110T150144Z
LOCATION:Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art
URL:https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2447850-wellness-walk
