BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441817-garlands-greenery-open-house-at-wylie-house-museum"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Garlands & Greenery Open House at Wylie House Museum
DTSTART:20261205T150000Z
DTEND:20261205T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261006T160213Z
UID:20261205T150000Z-2441817@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261205T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1667,1667/33439_garlands_and_greenery_livewhale_square.re
 v.1794617111.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Community events
DESCRIPTION:Wander through the historic house at your own pace\, surrounde
 d by fresh greenery and traditional holiday decorations. Costumed staff wi
 ll be on hand to welcome you\, share stories\, and answer questions.  Enjo
 y live music throughout the day\, featuring the Dickens Carolers\, IU stud
 ent musicians and á cappella groups\, and the Horseshoe Bend String Band.
  In the Museum's Education Center\, warm up with hot cider and cocoa\, enj
 oy holiday cookies\, and try your hand at family-friendly craft activities
 .  Come celebrate the season with music\, merriment\, and the timeless bea
 uty of Wylie House Museum! No registration required.Parking: Designated\, 
 free Wylie House parking spots are located behind the museum and education
  center\, accessible via the alley. Free street parking is located directl
 y in front of the museum on 2nd St. and is permissible on Saturdays in all
  the area neighborhood residential zoned spaces.Accessibility: The museum 
 has accessible parking next to the museum's Morton C. Bradley\, Jr. Educat
 ion Center\, with a path that leads to a ramp at the back door entrance of
  the museum. While the historic home's second floor is only accessible by 
 staircase\, digital images and virtual tour options are provided for visit
 ors who cannot visit the second floor. Please contact us in advance of you
 r visit to discuss any specific needs.  **********************************
 ***********************************************  Looking for a fully guide
 d tour of the historic home? Visit Wylie House Museum on Friday\, December
  4 (https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441814-winter-holiday-tours-at-
 wylie-house-museum)\; Friday\, December 11 (https://events.iu.edu/librarie
 s/event/2441815-winter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-house-museum)\; or Saturday
 \, December 12 (https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441816-winter-holid
 ay-tours-at-wylie-house-museum). Free holiday season tours are offered at 
 the top of each hour from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, with the final tour beginnin
 g at 3 p.m.
GEO:39.161697;-86.5309
LAST-MODIFIED:20261105T200254Z
LOCATION:WYLIE HOUSE (307 E. SECOND STREET)
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441817-garlands-greenery-open-h
 ouse-at-wylie-house-museum
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Wander through the historic house at you
 r own pace\, surrounded by fresh greenery and traditional holiday decorati
 ons. Costumed staff will be on hand to welcome you\, share stories\, and a
 nswer questions.</p><p>  Enjoy live music throughout the day\, featuring t
 he Dickens Carolers\, IU student musicians and á cappella groups\, and th
 e Horseshoe Bend String Band. In the Museum's Education Center\, warm up w
 ith hot cider and cocoa\, enjoy holiday cookies\, and try your hand at fam
 ily-friendly craft activities.</p><p>  Come celebrate the season with musi
 c\, merriment\, and the timeless beauty of Wylie House Museum! No registra
 tion required.</p><p><strong>Parking:</strong> Designated\, free Wylie Hou
 se parking spots are located behind the museum and education center\, acce
 ssible via the alley. Free street parking is located directly in front of 
 the museum on 2nd St. and is permissible on Saturdays in all the area neig
 hborhood residential zoned spaces.</p><p><strong>Accessibility:</strong> T
 he museum has accessible parking next to the museum's Morton C. Bradley\, 
 Jr. Education Center\, with a path that leads to a ramp at the back door e
 ntrance of the museum. While the historic home's second floor is only acce
 ssible by staircase\, digital images and virtual tour options are provided
  for visitors who cannot visit the second floor. Please contact us in adva
 nce of your visit to discuss any specific needs.</p><p>  *****************
 ****************************************************************<br />  Lo
 oking for a fully guided tour of the historic home? Visit Wylie House Muse
 um on <a href="https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441814-winter-holida
 y-tours-at-wylie-house-museum">Friday\, December 4</a>\; <a href="https://
 events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441815-winter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-house-
 museum">Friday\, December 11</a>\; or <a href="https://events.iu.edu/libra
 ries/event/2441816-winter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-house-museum">Saturday\, 
 December 12</a>. Free holiday season tours are offered at the top of each 
 hour from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, with the final tour beginning at 3 p.m.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Wylie House Museum\, <a href="mailto:libwy
 lie@iu.edu">libwylie@iu.edu</a>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
