X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DTSTART:20261205T190000Z
DTEND:20261205T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261103T094746Z
UID:20261205T190000Z-2471909@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261205T190000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,500,404/33239_Picasso_69.55_web.rev.1794617127.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Spark your creative writing through close looking and conversa
 tion. Together\, we'll explore the observations and questions sparked by t
 his painting\, then allow individual time for reflective writing to each b
 ring our own perspective.&#160\;  Whether you're a writer or simply curiou
 s to try something new\, you'll find inspiration here and a welcoming comm
 unity to share the journey.  What to Bringyour favorite pencil (no pens). 
  a notebook or paper. Clipboards are available to borrow.  a phone or came
 ra to take a picture of the art for later reference.    &#160\;Know Before
  You GoArrive early\, check in\, and get ready for an on-time start.Readwh
 ere to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.Abo
 ut Your Facilitator  Dedaimia Whitney earned an MFA in fiction from Indian
 a University under the direction of Scott Russell Sanders. She taught crea
 tive writing at Franklin College for many years. She has served the museum
  as a docent since 2019. Her favorite works of art are those that are both
  visually stimulating and thought-provoking.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T144746Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2461721-writing-in-the-galleries
