LOCATION:IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology\, 416 N. Indiana Ave.\
 , Bloomington\, IN 47408
GEO:39.170023;-86.526132
SUMMARY:Community Flow with Vibe Yoga - December
DESCRIPTION:Start your morning with a relaxing yoga class. This program w
 ill be recurring monthly throughout the fall semester.Event Details:    J
 oin Vibe Yoga at the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology for a free
 -to-attend flow to connect with the community and find a space that feels
  grounded\, safe\, and gently energizing. This class is beginner friendly
  and welcomes all experience levels.      These classes are designed arou
 nd vinyasa\, seamlessly moving form pose into the next. Often referred to
  as a moving meditation\, vinyasa means to "place in a special way." The 
 practice helps us flow toward our most vibrant life.  Pre-registration is
  required at vibeyogastudio.com (http://vibeyogastudio.com)    Located at
  the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology    Virgil T. Devault Progr
 ams Room (Room 111)    416 N Indiana Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47408      Th
 is class will occur monthly at 10am on:    Tuesday\, September 29    Tues
 day\, October 13    Tuesday\, November 10    Tuesday\, December 8  Parkin
 g Information:  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of th
 e Museum entrance (https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA) off Indiana
  Avenue. Free street parking is available in surrounding neighborhoods on
  weekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM.  Paid parking is also available in 
 the University Collections at McCalla (https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDe
 CACruHA) parking lot off Indiana Avenue and the Indiana Memorial Union (h
 ttps://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA) visitor lot.  Metered street pa
 rking is available near Sample Gates and throughout downtown Bloomington\
 , including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\, N
 orth Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Question
 s?  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, please r
 each out to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu) or (8
 12) 855-1696.Note:  By attending this event\, you agree to be in photogra
 phy that may be used by the University for promotional purposes. If you w
 ould not like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff memb
 er and they will inform assigned photographers of your request. If you se
 e that your image has been used in error\, please reach out to iumaa@iu.e
 du (mailto:iumaa@iu.edu) to request that it be taken down.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Start your morning with a relaxing yoga
  class. This program will be recurring monthly throughout the fall semest
 er.</p><p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p><div class="ewa-rteLine"><p>
     Join Vibe Yoga at the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology for a
  free-to-attend flow to connect with the community and find a space that 
 feels grounded\, safe\, and gently energizing. This class is beginner fri
 endly and welcomes all experience levels.  </p><p>    These classes are d
 esigned around vinyasa\, seamlessly moving form pose into the next. Often
  referred to as a moving meditation\, vinyasa means to "place in a specia
 l way." The practice helps us flow toward our most vibrant life.  </p><p>
 <strong>Pre-registration is required at <a href="http://vibeyogastudio.co
 m">vibeyogastudio.com</a></strong></p><p>    Located at the IU Museum of 
 Archaeology and Anthropology<br />    Virgil T. Devault Programs Room (Ro
 om 111)<br />    416 N Indiana Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47408  </p><p>    T
 his class will occur monthly at 10am on:<br />    Tuesday\, September 29<
 br />    Tuesday\, October 13<br />    Tuesday\, November 10<br />    Tue
 sday\, December 8  </p></div><p><strong>Parking Information:</strong></p>
 <p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Limited complimentary parking is available in
  front of the <a class="external" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst
 2gSW5fUA">Museum entrance</a> off Indiana Avenue. Free street parking is 
 available in surrounding neighborhoods on weekends and weekdays after 5:0
 0 PM.</p><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Paid parking is also available in th
 e <a class="external" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA">Un
 iversity Collections at McCalla</a> parking lot off Indiana Avenue and th
 e <a class="external" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA">In
 diana Memorial Union</a> visitor lot.</p><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Mete
 red street parking is available near Sample Gates and throughout downtown
  Bloomington\, including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4
 th Street\, North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant St
 reet.</p><p><strong>Questions?</strong></p><p>  For accessibility assista
 nce or questions about this event\, please reach out to Camden Hill at <a
  href="mailto:camrhill@iu.edu">camrhill@iu.edu</a> or (812) 855-1696.</p>
 <p><strong>Note:</strong></p><p>  By attending this event\, you agree to 
 be in photography that may be used by the University for promotional purp
 oses. If you would not like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Mus
 eum staff member and they will inform assigned photographers of your requ
 est. If you see that your image has been used in error\, please reach out
  to <a href="mailto:iumaa@iu.edu">iumaa@iu.edu</a> to request that it be 
 taken down.</p>
