BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 261": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2236919-micro-mythologies-world-mythology-made-miniature"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_261
SUMMARY:Micro-mythologies: World Mythology Made Miniature
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTSTAMP:20260312T103247Z
UID:20261114T050000Z-2236919@events.iu.edu__20261210
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1900,1900/30479_micromythologies_LW_avatar.rev.1773325700
 .png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:"Myths are the world's dreams."- Joseph Campbell.To believe is
  to be human.One of the greatest forces known to humankind\,belief is a un
 iversal impetus\, one that has raised and toppled temples\, instigated and
  eased wars\, and inspired written works\, both monumental and miniature. 
 This exhibition showcases a selection of minute materials that pertain to 
 mythologies and belief systems from across the world. From ancient Mesopot
 amian myth to modern Native American spirituality\, belief transcends time
  and history and intertwines human existence within our world.Micro-Mythol
 ogies: World Mythology Made Miniature is a miniature book exhibition which
  seeks to highlight some of our oldest and most powerful stories\, as well
  as those who preserved them.Mythological influence has shaped the world a
 round us. Whether that be through architecture\, art\, or literature\, myt
 hs serve as a testament to human cultural memory and the preservation of i
 ntangible tradition. Myths pull back the curtain of the past and reunite u
 s with the beliefs and stories of our ancestors.Most of these materials or
 iginate from the collection of prolific miniature book collector\, Ruth El
 izabeth Adomeit (1910-1996). Notable book artists highlighted inMicro-Myth
 ologies include Maryline Poole Adams\, Carol Cunningham\, Barbara J. Raheb
 \, Dianne Weiss\, and Gabrielle Fox.Micro-Mythologies: World Mythology Mad
 e Miniature is curated by Curatorial Assistant Jake Gentry\, with counsel 
 from Sarah McElroy Mitchell\, Curator of Religious Collections. In additio
 n\, exhibition design was done by Jenny Mack and graphic design by David O
 rr. This exhibition is on display in the Lilly Library Ball Room through D
 ecember 2026.
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T194733Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2236919-micro-mythologies-world-
 mythology-made-miniature
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="auto">"</span><i><spa
 n data-contrast="auto">Myths are the world's dreams</span></i><span data-c
 ontrast="auto">."- Joseph Campbell.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;20
 1341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335551550&quot\;:2\,&quot\;335551620&quot\;:2\,&q
 uot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><
 p><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot
 \;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><strong><i><span 
 data-contrast="auto">To believe is to be human</span></i></strong><span da
 ta-contrast="auto">.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:
 0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span>
 </p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201
 341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;
 :288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">One of the greatest forces
  known to humankind\,</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">belief </span></
 i><span data-contrast="auto">is a universal impetus\, one that has raised 
 and toppled temples\, instigated and eased wars\, and inspired written wor
 ks\, both monumental and miniature. This exhibition showcases a selection 
 of minute materials that pertain to mythologies and belief systems from ac
 ross the world. From ancient Mesopotamian myth to modern Native American s
 pirituality\, belief transcends time and history and intertwines human exi
 stence within our world.</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Micro-Mytholo
 gies: World Mythology Made Miniature </span></i><span data-contrast="auto"
 >is a miniature book exhibition which seeks to highlight some of our oldes
 t and most powerful stories\, as well as those who preserved them.</span><
 span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:1
 6777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="
 auto"></span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;3355
 57856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span d
 ata-contrast="auto">Mythological influence has shaped the world around us.
  Whether that be through architecture\, art\, or literature\, myths serve 
 as a testament to human cultural memory and the preservation of intangible
  tradition. Myths pull back the curtain of the past and reunite us with th
 e beliefs and stories of our ancestors.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot
 \;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&q
 uot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></span><span data-ccp
 -props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quo
 t\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">Most of
  these materials originate from the collection of prolific miniature book 
 collector\, Ruth Elizabeth Adomeit (1910-1996). Notable book artists highl
 ighted in</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Micro-Mythologies </span></i
 ><span data-contrast="auto">include Maryline Poole Adams\, Carol Cunningha
 m\, Barbara J. Raheb\, Dianne Weiss\, and Gabrielle Fox.</span><span data-
 ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&
 quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto"></sp
 an><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot
 \;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><i><span data-con
 trast="auto">Micro-Mythologies: World Mythology Made Miniature </span></i>
 <span data-contrast="auto">is curated by Curatorial Assistant Jake Gentry
 \, with counsel from Sarah McElroy Mitchell\, Curator of Religious Collect
 ions. In addition\, exhibition design was done by Jenny Mack and graphic d
 esign by David Orr. This exhibition is on display in the Lilly Library Bal
 l Room through December 2026.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;20134198
 3&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}
 "></span></p>
