X-SOURCE-ID:visit_bloomington
SUMMARY:The Great Arch | Arthouse Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261211T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261211T210000
UID:331707f7181f0ae44e25a572a2fbe20b@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:1983. French President Mitterrand decides to launch an interna
 tional architectural competition for the flagship project of his mandate: 
 the Great Arch of La Défense\, aligned with the Louvre and the Arc de Tri
 omphe. Against all odds\, Otto von Spreckelsen\, a Danish architect\, wins
  the competition. Overnight\, this 53-year-old man\, unknown in France\, a
 rrives in Paris where he is propelled to the helm of this pharaonic projec
 t. While the architect intends to build the Great Arch exactly as he envis
 ioned\, his ideas quickly clash with realistic constraints and the vicissi
 tudes of politics. [104 min\; drama\; English\, French\, and Dutch with En
 glish subtitles]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-great-arch-arthouse-now/602
 00/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
