 n. The BFA Thesis Exhibitions represent the culmination of each student's 
 undergraduate research in the arts. Students will work with the gallery to
  plan and install their thesis work. The exhibition will feature artwork b
 y students graduating with a concentration in a variety of studio areas: g
 raphic design\, painting\, photography\, and sculpture.Exhibition: Tuesday
 \, December 1–Friday\, December 11.Grunwald Gallery hours: Tuesday–Sat
 urday\, 12–4pm. Closed Sunday and Monday.Exhibiting BFA studentsAngelee:
  Photography  Olaleye Baker: Graphic Design  Lauren Brewster: Painting  Ma
 rilyn King: Graphic Design  Hayley Kline: Graphic Design  Harper Masson: G
 raphic Design  Kinsey Temple: Graphic Design  Nate Terrell: Sculpture  Tor
 yn White: Sculpture
