SUMMARY:Winter Holiday Tours at Wylie House Museum
DTSTART:20261212T150000Z
DTEND:20261212T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261006T160026Z
UID:20261212T150000Z-2441816@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261212T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2120/32920_Snowy_Wylie_Feb_2021_00.rev.1791316059.jp
 g
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Community events
DESCRIPTION:The historic 1835 home is adorned with fresh greenery and seas
 onal décor\, while tours bring Wylie family stories and holiday tradition
 s to life.  Tours begin at the top of each hour\, with the final tour begi
 nning at 3 p.m.  No registration is needed\, but we ask that groups of 8 o
 r more contact us in advance at libwylie@iu.edu (mailto:libwylie@iu.edu) o
 r (812) 855-6224.Parking: Designated\, free Wylie House parking spots are 
 located behind the museum and education center\, accessible via the alley.
  Free street parking is located directly in front of the museum on 2nd St.
  and is permissible on Saturdays in all the area neighborhood residential 
 zoned spaces.Accessibility: The museum has accessible parking next to the 
 museum's Morton C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center\, with a path that leads
  to a ramp at the back door entrance of the museum. While the historic hom
 e's second floor is only accessible by staircase\, digital images and virt
 ual tour options are provided for visitors who cannot visit the second flo
 or. Please contact us in advance of your visit to discuss any specific nee
 ds.  *********************************************************************
 ************  Looking to celebrate the season with music\, merriment\, and
  the timeless beauty of the historic home? Join Wylie House Museum for its
  festive Garlands &amp\; Greenery Open House on Saturday\, December 5\, fr
 om 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. This free\, drop-in event invites you to experience t
 he museum adorned for the holiday season.
GEO:39.161697;-86.5309
LAST-MODIFIED:20261111T195241Z
LOCATION:WYLIE HOUSE (307 E. SECOND STREET)
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441816-winter-holiday-tours-at-
 wylie-house-museum
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span class="TextRun SCXW253058102 BCX4" l
 ang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="NormalTextR
 un SCXW253058102 BCX4">The historic 1835 home is adorned with fresh greene
 ry and seasonal décor\, while tours bring Wylie family stories and holida
 y traditions to life.</span></span></p><p>  Tours begin at the top of each
  hour\, with the final tour beginning at 3 p.m.</p><p>  No registration is
  needed\, but we ask that groups of 8 or more contact us in advance at <a 
 href="mailto:libwylie@iu.edu">libwylie@iu.edu</a> or (812) 855-6224.</p><p
 ><strong>Parking:</strong> Designated\, free Wylie House parking spots are
  located behind the museum and education center\, accessible via the alley
 . Free street parking is located directly in front of the museum on 2nd St
 . and is permissible on Saturdays in all the area neighborhood residential
  zoned spaces.</p><p><strong>Accessibility:</strong> The museum has access
 ible parking next to the museum's Morton C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center
 \, with a path that leads to a ramp at the back door entrance of the museu
 m. While the historic home's second floor is only accessible by staircase
 \, digital images and virtual tour options are provided for visitors who c
 annot visit the second floor. Please contact us in advance of your visit t
 o discuss any specific needs.</p><p>  ************************************
 *********************************************<br />  Looking to celebrate 
 the season with music\, merriment\, and the timeless beauty of the histori
 c home? Join Wylie House Museum for its festive <a href="https://events.iu
 .edu/libraries/event/2441817-garlands-greenery-open-house-at-wylie-house-m
 useum"><em>Garlands &amp\; Greenery Open House</em></a> on Saturday\, Dece
 mber 5\, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m. This free\, drop-in event invites you to e
 xperience the museum adorned for the holiday season.</p>
