X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Mathematics as a Medium: Art\, Practice\, and Inquiry | Symposium
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
DTSTAMP:20261113T180855Z
UID:20270115T180000Z-2484592@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20270115
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/33570_segerman_henry_osuma-square-768x768.rev.1794
 617101.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:This symposium&#160\;seeks to redefine the genre of mathematic
 al art\, welcome an international cohort of its practitioners\, and identi
 fy IUB as a leading site for interdisciplinary dialogue between mathematic
 s and the arts.  Organized by Eskenazi School Associate Professor of Inter
 ior Design Jiangmei Wu\, who also curated the exhibition\, and Professor o
 f Mathematics Kevin Pilgrim\, the symposium starts Friday\, January 15 at 
