BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Comedy Attic": "https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/387449"}
X-SOURCE-ID:comedy_attic
SUMMARY:An Evening With Phil Hanley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270115T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270115T210000
UID:20270115-an-evening-with-phil-hanley-1900
DESCRIPTION:Originally from Oshawa\, Canada\, Phil is now a key figure in 
 the NYC comedy scene\, performing regularly at the Comedy Cellar. With nea
 rly 650K followers on Instagram and nearly 400K followers and 15.6 milli
 on likes on TikTok\, he’s appeared on major late-night shows like The T
 onight Show \, Late Night with Seth Meyers \, and The Late Late Show . Han
 ley’s memoir\, SPELLBOUND: My Life as a Dyslexic \, chronicles his lifel
 ong struggle with dyslexia and how comedy became his saving grace. Hanley
 ’s goal in writing this book is to continue his advocacy for dyslexia aw
 areness and his commitment to using his platform to inspire others and pro
 mote a deeper understanding of neurodiversity. He also self-released his s
 tand-up special\, Ooh La La \, on YouTube (where he has nearly 675k follo
 wers)\, which has amassed over 2 million views . Additionally\, Phil was f
 eatured in the film I Feel Pretty and the Comedy Central series Inside Amy
  Schumer \, with his half-hour special available on Comedy Central and iTu
 nes. His 2018 album\, Please Don’t Chit Chat While I’m Pursuing My Dre
 am \, is a fan favorite.
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/387449
X-SOURCE:The Comedy Attic
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 135": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2457776-lecture-a-failure-of-will-why-cyber-operations"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_135
SUMMARY:Lecture: A Failure of Will: Why Cyber Operations Against Ukraine's
  and Poland's Energy Systems Go Unanswered with Szymon Skalski
DTSTART:20270115T190000Z
DTEND:20270115T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261021T162006Z
UID:20270115T190000Z-2459414@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20270115T190000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/181/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,225,225/33172_Skalski.rev.1794617131.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Cyber operations against power grids and heating systems recur
  in war and outside it. The same conduct falls under the law of armed conf
 lict in one setting\, peacetime international law in the other. Drawing on
  Russian operations in Ukraine and Poland\, this lecture asks why correct 
 legal classification so rarely brings consequences.  Szymon Skalski is a d
 octoral candidate at Jagiellonian University and Visiting Scholar at IU's 
 Ostrom Workshop\, where he leads its working group on environmental securi
 ty and technological risk in conflict. His research interests include cybe
 rsecurity of critical infrastructure\, global security\, and liability for
  cyberattacks.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20261021T202006Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2457776-lecture-a-failure-of-will-wh
 y-cyber-operations
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">C
 yber operations against power grids and heating systems recur in war and o
 utside it. The same conduct falls under the law of armed conflict in one s
 etting\, peacetime international law in the other. Drawing on Russian oper
 ations in Ukraine and Poland\, this lecture asks why correct legal classif
 ication so rarely brings consequences.</span></p><p class="x_elementToProo
 f" data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">  Szymon Skalski is a doctoral candi
 date at Jagiellonian University and Visiting Scholar at IU's Ostrom Worksh
 op\, where he leads its working group on environmental security and techno
 logical risk in conflict. His research interests include cybersecurity of 
 critical infrastructure\, global security\, and liability for cyberattacks
 .</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2459414
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/181/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,225\,225/33172_Skalski.rev.1794617131.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Lecturer Szymon <span data-olk-copy-source="Mess
 ageBody">Skalski\, a doctoral candidate at Jagiellonian University and Vis
 iting Scholar at IU's Ostrom Workshop</span>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
END:VEVENT
