DESCRIPTION:This symposium&#160\;seeks to redefine the genre of mathematic
 al art\, welcome an international cohort of its practitioners\, and identi
 fy IUB as a leading site for interdisciplinary dialogue between mathematic
 s and the arts.  Organized by Eskenazi School Associate Professor of Inter
 ior Design Jiangmei Wu\, who also curated the exhibition\, and Professor o
 f Mathematics Kevin Pilgrim\, the symposium starts Friday\, January 15 at 
 noon and continues through Saturday afternoon.  Over three keynotes\, them
 atic panels\, and workshops\, participating artists\, designers\, mathemat
 icians\, and scholars will explore mathematics as an active medium of crea
 tive practice and create a shared space for exchange among disciplines.Vis
 it here for more information about the exhibition. (https://eskenazi.india
 na.edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium.html)V
 isit here for the symposium schedule. (https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events
 /special-events/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium-symposium.html)This projec
 t was supported by Indiana University's Presidential Arts and Humanities P
 rogram\; the Office for Research Development\, Indiana University Research
 \; and also at Indiana University Bloomington: Eskenazi School of Art\, Ar
 chitecture + Design\; Department of Mathematics\; and Luddy School of Info
 rmatics\, Computing and Engineering Artificial Intelligence Center (LAIC).
