BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2484593-mathematics-as-a-medium-exhibition"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Mathematics as a Medium | Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTSTAMP:20261113T180929Z
UID:20270117T050000Z-2484593@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;VALUE=DATE:20270117
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/33570_segerman_henry_osuma-square-768x768.rev.1794
 617101.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:Exhibition Opening Reception: January 15\, 6:30–8:30 pmExhib
 ition Dates: January 15–March 6Symposium Dates: January 15–16  Curated
  by Associate Professor of Interior Design in the Eskenazi School of Art\,
  Architecture + Design Jiangmei Wu\, the exhibition "Mathematics as a Medi
 um" opening Friday\, January 15 at Indiana University's Grunwald Gallery o
 f Art complements a symposium January 15 and 16 convening many of the exhi
 bitors with counterparts from across the international mathematical art co
 mmunity. Over three keynotes\, thematic panels\, and workshops\, participa
 ting artists\, designers\, mathematicians\, and scholars will explore math
 ematics as an active medium of creative practice and create a shared space
  for exchange among disciplines.  The coordinated events seek to usher in 
 a broader understanding of the relationship between mathematics and art. P
 roceeding from the proposition that mathematics is a mediumsuch as paint\,
  stone\, or sound—through which artists and designers create and culture
 s express themselves\, the exhibition and symposium are designed more broa
 dly to redefine mathematics as a living\, generative practice that shapes 
 how we think\, make\, and experience the world.Visit here for more informa
 tion about the exhibition. (https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/exhibitions/grunw
 ald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium.html)Visit here for the sympos
 ium schedule. (https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events/special-events/upcoming
 /2027-01-15-math-medium-symposium.html)This project was supported by India
 na University's Presidential Arts and Humanities Program\; the Office for 
 Research Development\, Indiana University Research\; and also at Indiana U
 niversity Bloomington: Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design\; De
 partment of Mathematics\; and Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing and 
 Engineering Artificial Intelligence Center (LAIC).
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
LAST-MODIFIED:20261113T233038Z
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 4740
 5
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2484593-mathematics-as-a-medium-e
 xhibition
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="p1"><strong>Exhibition Opening Rece
 ption:</strong> January 15\, 6:30–8:30 pm<br /><strong>Exhibition Dates<
 /strong>: January 15–March 6<br /><strong>Symposium Dates:</strong> Janu
 ary 15–16</p><p class="p1">  Curated by Associate Professor of Interior 
 Design in the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design Jiangmei Wu\,
  the exhibition "Mathematics as a Medium" opening Friday\, January 15 at I
 ndiana University's Grunwald Gallery of Art complements a symposium Januar
 y 15 and 16 convening many of the exhibitors with counterparts from across
  the international mathematical art community. Over three keynotes\, thema
 tic panels\, and workshops\, participating artists\, designers\, mathemati
 cians\, and scholars will explore mathematics as an active medium of creat
 ive practice and create a shared space for exchange among disciplines.</p>
 <p class="p1">  The coordinated events seek to usher in a broader understa
 nding of the relationship between mathematics and art. Proceeding from the
  proposition that mathematics is a medium—such as paint\, stone\, or sou
 nd—through which artists and designers create and cultures express thems
 elves\, the exhibition and symposium are designed more broadly to redefine
  mathematics as a living\, generative practice that shapes how we think\, 
 make\, and experience the world.</p><p><a href="https://eskenazi.indiana.e
 du/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium.html" targ
 et="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit here for more information about the exhib
 ition.</a></p><p class="p1"><a href="https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events/s
 pecial-events/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium-symposium.html" target="_bla
 nk" rel="noopener">Visit here for the symposium schedule.</a></p><p class=
 "p1"><em>This project was supported by Indiana University's Presidential A
 rts and Humanities Program\; the Office for Research Development\, Indiana
  University Research\; and also at Indiana University Bloomington: Eskenaz
 i School of Art\, Architecture + Design\; Department of Mathematics\; and 
 Luddy School of Informatics\, Computing and Engineering Artificial Intelli
 gence Center (LAIC).</em></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div>\n  Yaël Ksander\n</div>\n<div>\n  Director
  of Communications and Marketing\n</div>\n<div>\n  Eskenazi School of Art
 \, Architecture + Design\n</div>\n<div>\n  <a href="mailto:yksander@iu.edu
 ">yksander@iu.edu</a>\n</div>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2484593
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height
 /168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,768\,768/33570_segerman_henry_osuma-square-76
 8x768.rev.1794617101.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:<p class="p1">\n  Henry Segerman\, "Untitled" (d
 etail). Stereographic projections\, 3D printing\, 2025\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p class="p1">\n  An exhibition being held in tandem w
 ith a two-day symposium on the IU Bloomington campus in January 2027.\n</p
 >
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Arts and Humanities|Bloomington|Computing and Engineering
  Artificial Intelligence Center|Department of Mathematics|Eskenazi School|
 Grunwald Gallery|IU Research|Luddy School|Mathematics as a Medium|Office f
