BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncounty.com/events/pam-tillis-lorrie-morgan/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Pam Tillis & Lorrie Morgan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270129T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270129T200000
DTSTAMP:20261027T162142Z
UID:MEC-0681d00eafecdd22216de8277b005334@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270129T200000
SEQUENCE:3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 10/2-300x240-12.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Live Music
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261027
DESCRIPTION:Pam Tillis and Lorrie Morgan are currently delighting old and 
 new fans across North America on their highly successful Grits and Glamour
  Tour. Veteran recording artists and performers\, they grace the country f
 ormat with style\, flair\, and undeniable talent that is captivating and t
 imeless\, and will make a stop at the Brown County Music Center in Nashvil
 le\, Ind.\nFormed in 2009\, the Grits and Glamour tour is a “together is
  better” event. The show is only loosely scripted. Good-natured ribbing 
 and off-the-cuff remarks are just part of the fun. They add tight harmonie
 s to each other’s material\, classic songs like Tillis’ “Maybe It Wa
 s Memphis\,” and “Mi Vida Loca\,” and Morgan’s “Something In Red
 ” and “Except for Monday” as well as new and original music from mor
 e recent recordings. The ladies are backed by some of Nashville’s finest
  musicians and singers.\nTheir career highlights are numerous and varied. 
 Combined\, they have recorded 28 top 10 hits\, more than 18 million record
 s sold\, and 12 number one songs. There have been Grammys\, CMA Awards\, m
 ovie credits\, television appearances\, and Broadway performances. They ha
 ve rocked arenas\, helmed world-class symphonies\, and toured on almost ev
 ery continent. These 50- somethings are more than a little flattered that 
 they can still sell out shows\, turn heads\, and make hearts beat fast nea
 rly four decades into their careers. It’s almost unnecessary to point ou
 t how rare it is to have such long-term success in an industry so fickle\,
  but Pam Tillis and Lorrie Morgan haven’t missed a beat. In fact\, they 
 both maintain extensive solo touring schedules\, enhanced by the buzz that
  surrounds the Grits and Glamour tour.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Music Center":MAILTO:boxoffice@browncountymusic
 center.com
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/pam-tillis-lorrie-morgan/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
