X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2468679-writing-in-the-galleries"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DTSTART:20270206T190000Z
DTEND:20270206T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261103T094744Z
UID:20270206T190000Z-2471903@events.iu.edu__20270206
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/29305_Writing_in_the_Galleries_-_thumbnail.rev.
 1767371047.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Spark your creative writing through close looking and conversa
 tion.&#160\;Whether you're a writer or simply curious to try something new
 \, you'll find inspiration here and a welcoming community to share the jou
 rney.  What to Bringyour favorite pencil (no pens).  a notebook or paper. 
 Clipboards are available to borrow.  a phone or camera to take a picture o
 f the art for later reference.  Know Before You GoArrive early\, check in
 \, and get ready for an on-time start.Readwhere to find us\, where to park
 \, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.About Your Facilitator  Dedaimia 
 Whitney earned an MFA in fiction from Indiana University under the directi
 on of Scott Russell Sanders. She taught creative writing at Franklin Colle
 ge for many years. She has served the museum as a docent since 2019. Her f
 avorite works of art are those that are both visually stimulating and thou
 ght-provoking.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T144744Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2468679-writing-in-the-galleries
