X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 343": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2368531-global-competencies-skills-development-series"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_343
X-SOURCE:IU Kelley School of Business
DTSTART:20270305T150000Z
DTEND:20270305T170000Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: International Cris
 is Response Simulation — Leading Under Pressure
DESCRIPTION:Master the Tradecraft of Crisis Leadership  When internationa
 l crises break\, leaders don't have the luxury of complete information or
  total control. They have to make rapid strategic calls\, counter targete
 d disinformation in real time\, and align rival organizations under inten
 se scrutiny.  Skip the slides and build actual operational skills in Inte
 rnational Crisis Response\, an interactive\, multi-agency simulation desi
 gned to test and sharpen your leadership under realistic pressure.  Guide
 d by Michael Jack\, certified leadership coach\, international disaster s
 trategist\, and former USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Division 
 Director\, this hands-on session pushes you beyond theory into real-world
  strategic execution.  Core Skills You'll Walk Away WithRapid Strategic D
 ecision-Making: Practice making consequential\, high-level decisions unde
 r extreme time pressure and incomplete data.    Crisis Communications &am
 p\; Disinformation Defense: Learn how to deliver disciplined messaging un
 der scrutiny\, navigate press briefings\, and actively counter viral fake
  news.    Cross-Organizational Negotiation: Master coalition-building and
  gap-filling across international teams\, host governments\, UN bodies\, 
 and non-profits whose interests may compete with your own.    Leadership 
 Resilience &amp\; Trauma Management: Gain practical tools for managing st
 aff decision fatigue\, operational stress\, and team performance during p
 rolonged high-pressure events.      Dynamic Roleplay Structure  You'll be
  embedded directly into key crisis response teams—representing U.S. Emb
 assy officials\, UN agencies\, international NGOs\, host government autho
 rities\, and global media correspondents—responding live as dynamic sce
 nario "injects" unfold.  ߌࠗho Can Attend?Open to all: Undergrads\, Gra
 d Students\, Faculty\, Staff\, and Community Members. (Light snacks and d
 rinks provided)  Facilitator Bio  Michael Jack is a certified leadership 
 coach\, international crisis management strategist\, and former Division 
 Director at USAID's Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance. He has managed di
 saster responses across 80+ countries\, including the Iraq Sinjar crisis\
 , West Africa Ebola outbreak\, Mexico City earthquake\, South Sudan emerg
 ency\, Amazon wildfires\, and Northern Ethiopia response.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="13">  Master the Trad
 ecraft of Crisis Leadership</h4><p data-path-to-node="14">  When internat
 ional crises break\, leaders don't have the luxury of complete informatio
 n or total control. They have to make rapid strategic calls\, counter tar
 geted disinformation in real time\, and align rival organizations under i
 ntense scrutiny.</p><p data-path-to-node="15">  Skip the slides and build
  actual operational skills in <strong data-path-to-node="15" data-index-i
 n-node="55">International Crisis Response</strong>\, an interactive\, mul
 ti-agency simulation designed to test and sharpen your leadership under r
 ealistic pressure.</p><p data-path-to-node="16">  Guided by Michael Jack\
 , certified leadership coach\, international disaster strategist\, and fo
 rmer USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Division Director\, this ha
 nds-on session pushes you beyond theory into real-world strategic executi
 on.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Core Skills You'll Walk Away With</h4
 ><ul data-path-to-node="18"><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0"><strong d
 ata-path-to-node="18\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Rapid Strategic Decisi
 on-Making:</strong> Practice making consequential\, high-level decisions 
 under extreme time pressure and incomplete data.    </p></li><li><p data-
 path-to-node="18\,1\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,1\,0" data-index-i
 n-node="0">Crisis Communications &amp\; Disinformation Defense:</strong> 
 Learn how to deliver disciplined messaging under scrutiny\, navigate pres
 s briefings\, and actively counter viral fake news.    </p></li><li><p da
 ta-path-to-node="18\,2\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,2\,0" data-inde
 x-in-node="0">Cross-Organizational Negotiation:</strong> Master coalition
 -building and gap-filling across international teams\, host governments\,
  UN bodies\, and non-profits whose interests may compete with your own.  
   </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,3\,0"><strong data-path-to-node=
 "18\,3\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Leadership Resilience &amp\; Trauma Man
 agement:</strong> Gain practical tools for managing staff decision fatigu
 e\, operational stress\, and team performance during prolonged high-press
 ure events.    </p></li></ul><h4 data-path-to-node="19">  Dynamic Rolepla
 y Structure</h4><p data-path-to-node="20">  You'll be embedded directly i
 nto key crisis response teams—representing <strong data-path-to-node="2
 0" data-index-in-node="72">U.S. Embassy officials\, UN agencies\, interna
 tional NGOs\, host government authorities\, and global media corresponden
 ts</strong>—responding live as dynamic scenario "injects" unfold.</p><h
